+# W1 / Q97 managed-discovery resource contract — 2026-11-06
+
+**Disposition.** E506 records the locally derived Q97 contract for managed `fs_search` and `fs_reach`. The values below are implementation limits, not approved-host measurements. Q111-A remains binding: crossing an aggregate work/index/output/time budget is explicit non-success, never a partial or truncated success. Q134 resolved the existing per-file boundary: files above the established 200,000-byte indexing ceiling remain a declared exclusion, counted and surfaced as skipped; they do not by themselves turn an otherwise in-budget discovery into a budget refusal. This preserves the existing `skipped_large_files`/`files_skipped` contract. It does not permit silently dropping candidates that exceed any aggregate quota.
+
+## Selected limits
+
+| Resource | Exact managed-call bound | Enforcement / over-bound behavior |
+| --- | ---: | --- |
+| Walk inventory | 8,192 total directory + file entries; depth ≤64; relative path ≤512 UTF-8 bytes | Bounded `scandir` traversal; stop before retaining entry 8,193, descending past depth 64, or accepting a longer path; return nonretryable `search_failed` / `reach_failed`. |
+| Candidate inventory | ≤2,048 eligible candidate files per call, including oversized candidates that are explicitly excluded from indexing | Preflight before index/result growth; candidate 2,049 refuses the whole call. No truncation to the first 2,048. |
+| Per-file source/index | 200,000 bytes maximum indexed/read per file (existing ceiling); larger files are excluded and reported in bounded skip metadata | Rooted size/identity revalidation before read. Oversized files contribute to candidate count but not aggregate indexed-source bytes; do not parse/index them. |
+| Aggregate source | ≤33,554,432 bytes (32 MiB) across eligible files actually read/indexed in one call | Count validated source bytes before retaining/indexing each file. The first byte beyond the ceiling refuses the call; discard the in-memory index and all partial results. |
+| Reach AST work | ≤2,000,000 AST nodes total; ≤256,000 nodes in one file | Count nodes after parsing and before symbol/edge result accumulation. A per-file source ceiling bounds parser input; AST-node overflow is whole-call non-success. |
+| Reach index cardinality | ≤100,000 symbols and ≤250,000 call edges total; ≤25,000 edges from one file | Enforce before DB insertion/retention; overflow is whole-call non-success. |
+| Per-call index storage | SQLite page size 4,096 bytes; at most 32,768 pages = 134,217,728 bytes (128 MiB); page cache ≤16 MiB | Set and verify SQLite limits on the one-shot in-memory search/reach index; `SQLITE_FULL`/limit crossing maps to explicit non-success. No `.fa/fts.db` or persistent index. |
+| Memory reserve | 671,088,640 bytes (640 MiB) per active managed discovery call | Formula below. W3 must check approved profile `memory_bytes ≥1,342,177,280` (1,280 MiB): the 640 MiB call reserve plus an equal 640 MiB cell/worker headroom allowance. A lower profile blocks deployment of managed discovery; do not infer from test profiles. |
+| Serialized output | Full serialized ToolResult ≤30,000 ASCII bytes; full helper JSON envelope ≤61,440 bytes (60 KiB); cell reply frame ≤65,536 bytes total, including its 4-byte length prefix | Serialize the complete result with `ensure_ascii=True`, `allow_nan=False`, compact separators, and count bytes. Any overrun returns a small refusal envelope; no result trimming/retry. The inner result cap remains below the 32,768-byte tool-context ceiling. |
+| Request | Compact UTF-8 JSON tool request ≤65,536 bytes before dispatch | Reject before schema dispatch / helper allocation. The outer authenticated EXEC frame retains its existing protocol cap. |
+| Deadline | `min(parent EXEC absolute deadline, call_start_monotonic + 25,000 ms)` | Check before traversal, source reads, each index unit, and serialization. Parent deadline or helper deadline expiry is non-success (`command_timeout` only when timeout is confirmed); terminate/reap the one-shot helper, do not retry or publish partial output. |
+| Per-view concurrency | Exactly 1 active `fs_search` or `fs_reach` call for a view | Mark both discovery tools serial in the loop and retain the cell's one-active-operation gate. No unbounded queue; overlap is serialized before dispatch. |
+
+The existing user-selected search/reach result limits, depth semantics, and documented oversized-file exclusions remain ordinary tool semantics. They are distinct from these resource budgets. A query hitting a resource budget is not converted into the existing `truncated=true` success path.
+
+## Memory derivation
+
+A synthetic 200,000-byte dense-assignment source (`"x=0\n" * 50_000`) produced 200,001 AST nodes and a 124,499,768-byte `tracemalloc` peak while running `ast.parse` and `StructuralIndex._walk_tree`. A near-limit dense-call fixture (200,001 bytes; deliberately one byte over the source ceiling) produced 99,999 nodes, 24,999 edges, and a 72,512,020-byte peak. The larger fixture peak is the formula input `P=124,499,768`; local traced allocation is not host RSS and is not an approved production limit.
+
+`M_raw = 3P + 2S + I + D + C + O`, where `S=33,554,432` aggregate source bytes, `I=8,388,608` bounded candidate/path inventory allowance, `D=134,217,728` SQLite page ceiling, `C=16,777,216` SQLite cache ceiling, and `O=30,000` serialized ToolResult bytes. Thus `M_raw=600,021,720` bytes. Round **up** to the next 134,217,728-byte (128 MiB) quantum: `M_reserve=671,088,640` bytes = **640 MiB**. The factor of three on the synthetic peak is an explicit engineering margin; the source, index-page, cache, inventory, and output terms are separate caps, not inferred from RSS.
+
+The source corpus probe (local checkout only, not production authority) found 1,615 walk entries; 1,081 search candidates, of which 1,075 were within 200,000 bytes and contained 20,211,272 bytes; and 582 Python reach candidates, of which 581 were within the per-file ceiling and contained 8,127,896 bytes. The largest valid Python candidate was 196,504 bytes; `src/fa/execution/workspace.py` is 256,012 bytes and is therefore an explicit skipped file under Q134. The under-ceiling Python corpus contained 929,624 AST nodes, 8,698 function/async-function definitions, 737 classes, and 54,485 call nodes. These measurements justify that the selected candidate/source/AST/index-count ceilings exceed this source sample with headroom; they do not establish production parity, approved-profile identity, host memory behavior, or host acceptance.
+
+## Implementation and failure contract
+
+Managed-only discovery must use a bounded incremental `scandir` inventory rather than first materializing `os.walk`'s unbounded per-directory lists. Count the full walk inventory and candidate set before search-result growth; stat sizes during preflight, then verify identities and actual byte counts through `RootedFileReader` as files are read. Keep the index one-shot and in memory (`Path(":memory:")` / `in_memory=True`), enforce page/cache bounds, and close it on every exit. Preserve legacy host-mode behavior.
+
+Aggregate quota, rooted-read race, AST/cardinality/page, serialization, or deadline failure returns the existing `ToolResult` error shape with `search_failed` or `reach_failed`, stable sanitized reason, and `retryable=false`; it yields no paths/results for controller observation. Backend absence stays `execution_unavailable`; confirmed timeout stays `command_timeout`; uncertain identity, terminality, or transport stays `execution_unknown`. Search/reach output must never be shortened into success to satisfy a cap. Oversized per-file exclusions remain visible in the established skip field/count. No host Git, canonical project writes, second writer, host index, retry, or fallback is permitted.
+
+## Required verification (not yet run)
+
+- **C0:** exact-bound and cap+1 synthetic fixtures for walk entries, depth/path, candidate count, aggregate source bytes, AST nodes, symbol/edge rows, SQLite page/cache, deadline, request, and escaped-Unicode full-envelope bytes. Verify every resource overrun returns non-success before any partial result escapes; verify >200,000-byte files are reported as the selected exclusion and do not enter the index. Include dense 200,000-byte AST/call fixtures; do not assert local `tracemalloc` as production RSS.
+- **C1:** actual `fa run` → production role registry → managed handler → local `SupervisorService`/`WorkspaceAuthority` through the typed non-PTY cell helper. Assert exact view/grant/profile, one operation per call, same-view serialization, controller search observations only after valid complete success, zero host Git, no `.fa/fts.db`, no canonical mutation, and no partial result on each cap.
+- **Mutation:** kill pre-allocation/refusal producers and the caller edges binding the typed executor and serial scheduler; restore byte-identically and rerun exact nodeids before proceeding. Existing W1 S3P3 and R28 producer/EDGE targets remain required.
+- **DoD/boundary:** Q97 is locally recorded, not a host pass. W3 checks the approved profile/config against the stated memory threshold before deployment. Only W4 observes target-host cgroup/CPU/RSS/process behavior. No Docker or live-host evidence is claimed by this note.
